@* One drive bay card. Blu-ray/4K and DVD Movie Disc both open a
   mode-choice popup; Movie-Only MKV is disc-agnostic; DVD's popup has
   three real options (MakeMKV backup, Redumper raw ISO, Movie-Only).
   Every mode button is gated by the real detected disc Category. A
   Cancel button appears while running; Retry Last Rip appears after
   a completed operation -- now goes through BatchSyncService's gate
   the same as any other rip start, so it can't bypass Multi-Drive
   Batch Sync's concurrent-rip cap the way it previously could. The
   Open Output Folder button sits next to Eject/Close Tray. Bay title
   is click-to-rename and persists to config.json. Tray control tracks
   trayIsOpen as real app-managed state -- Eject is always available
   (opens an empty tray too), Close only once the tray is actually
   open. Shows real disc metadata and drive hardware info, plus an
   OmniDrive/LibreDrive compatibility badge with a persisted
   confirmation checkbox. Has a collapsible log console, and writes a
   CSV history record on every completed (non-cancelled) operation.

   Output naming: every ripping method names its output after the
   disc's real title, falling back to a DriveLetter_Tag_Timestamp
   scheme when no usable title exists, with a real duplicate-output
   confirmation guarding against silently overwriting a prior rip.
   PickMovieOnly specifically lets the user edit that suggested name
   in TrackPickerWindow before extraction starts -- MakeMKV still
   creates the file under its own auto-generated name as always, and
   MakeMkvService.RenameNewestMkv renames it to the chosen name
   afterward (picking the most-recently-written .mkv, not just the
   first one found, so a stale leftover file can't get renamed by
   mistake). Movie-Only output now always gets a real SHA1/MD5 (it
   didn't before), with the Redump *match* step correctly skipped --
   a re-muxed .mkv could never match Redump's raw-disc-dump database,
   so checking anyway would misleadingly read as a bad rip. DVD's
   MakeMKV-backup internal .iso filename now uses the same chosen
   name too, instead of a hardcoded DriveLetter-based one.

   Metadata & artwork: for movie/DVD discs, AutoFetchArtSilently()
   fires automatically on insert when no real cover image is cached
   yet (TMDB only -- skipped with a log line if no TMDB key is set). The cached poster shows inline as a base64 data URI. A "Show
   details" toggle reveals the cached description text.

   Multi-Drive Batch Sync / Unattended Mode: TryAutoStart() fires on
   disc insert when either config.UnattendedAutoStart or
   config.BatchQueueMode is on, gated through BatchSyncService's
   shared slot/queue when Multi-Drive Batch Sync is on. Every
   preflight check passes config.UnattendedAutoStart through globally.
   Full backups go into a size-based subfolder (BD-25 / BD-50 /
   DVD-5 / DVD-9) whenever Auto-categorize or Unattended Mode is on,
   and Movie-Only MKVs go into their own MKV subfolder. In Unattended
   Mode a name collision saves as "Title (2)" instead of overwriting. Every successful rip beeps (config.SoundAlerts) and, in Batch
   Queue Mode, bumps a per-drive "N DONE" session counter. Manual
   button clicks also go through the Multi-Drive Batch Sync gate
   (StartGated), same as auto-starts and Retry Last Rip.

   Game discs get a "File name" box on the bay. Typed before a dump,
   it names the output; changed during a dump (e.g. one that Batch
   Queue or Unattended Mode auto-started), the new name is applied
   when the dump finishes; after a dump, the Rename button renames the
   folder, every file in it, the .cue sheet's file references, and the
   History record.

   Original Xbox / Xbox 360 discs can't be identified before a dump
   (Windows can't see their game files), so after a game dump
   ApplyRedumperLogDetection() reads Redumper's log for its "XGD
   detected (version: N)" line, records the console, and moves a dump
   that landed in Games\General_Games into Games\<console>.

   Blu-ray Full Backup has an automatic ImgBurn stage 2 when ImgBurn
   is available. DVD's raw ISO dump falls back to ImgBurn when
   Redumper isn't found. *@

@implements IDisposable
@using System.Threading.Tasks
@using System.IO
@using System.Diagnostics

<div class="bay-card">
    @if (isEditingLabel)
    {
        <input class="label-input" @bind="labelDraft" @bind:event="oninput"
               @onkeydown="HandleLabelKeydown" autofocus />
        <button class="label-confirm-btn" @onclick="ConfirmLabel">✓</button>
    }
    else
    {
        <h2 style="cursor: pointer;" title="Click to rename" @onclick="StartEditLabel">
            @(customLabel ?? $"DRIVE BAY {DriveLetter}:")
        </h2>
    }
    <p class="bay-subtitle">Optical Ripping &amp; Decryption Module</p>

    @if (MediaPresent || !string.IsNullOrEmpty(DriveModel))
    {
        <p class="bay-meta">
            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(DriveModel))
            {
                <text>@DriveModel@(!string.IsNullOrEmpty(DriveFirmware) ? $" (FW {DriveFirmware})" : "")</text>
            }
            @if (MediaPresent && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(FormatLabel))
            {
                <text> • @FormatLabel • @CapacityLabel</text>
            }
            @if (MediaPresent && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(AacsVersion))
            {
                <text> • @AacsVersion</text>
            }
            @if (MediaPresent && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(EffectiveGameSystem))
            {
                <text> • @EffectiveGameSystem</text>
            }
            @if (MediaPresent && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Serial))
            {
                <text> • @Serial</text>
            }
        </p>
    }

    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(DriveModel))
    {
        <p class="bay-meta" style="margin-top: -6px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
            @if (OmnidriveCompatible == true)
            {
                <span style="color: var(--success);">✓ MT1959-compatible (flash unverified)</span>
            }
            else
            {
                <span>✕ Not on OmniDrive list</span>
            }
            <label style="cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px;">
                <input type="checkbox" checked="@omnidriveConfirmed" @onchange="ToggleOmnidriveConfirmed" />
                OmniDrive confirmed
            </label>
            @if (libreDriveSeen)
            {
                <span style="color: var(--success);">✓ LibreDrive mode (MakeMKV)</span>
            }
        </p>
    }

    @if (MediaPresent && (Category == DiscCategory.BluRay || Category == DiscCategory.Dvd || Category == DiscCategory.Game))
    {
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 4px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
            @if (coverDataUri is not null)
            {
                <img src="@coverDataUri" alt="Cover art"
                     style="width: 50px; height: 70px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); flex: 0 0 auto;" />
            }
            <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px;">
                <button class="bay-btn tray-btn" style="width: auto;" @onclick="FetchMetadata">
                    🎨 Fetch Metadata &amp; Artwork
                </button>
                @if (hasCachedCover && cachedArt?.Metadata is not null)
                {
                    <span class="tray-message" style="color: var(--success); cursor: pointer;"
                          @onclick="OpenArtCacheFolder" title="Click to open cached artwork folder">
                        ✓ Cached: @cachedArt.Metadata.Title (@cachedArt.Metadata.Source)
                    </span>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(cachedArt.Metadata.Detail))
                    {
                        <span class="tray-message" style="cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline;"
                              @onclick="() => showMetadataDetails = !showMetadataDetails">
                            @(showMetadataDetails ? "▾ Hide details" : "▸ Show details")
                        </span>
                    }
                }
            </div>
        </div>
        @if (showMetadataDetails && cachedArt?.Metadata is not null && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(cachedArt.Metadata.Detail))
        {
            <p class="bay-subtitle" style="margin: 0 0 8px; max-width: 100%;">@cachedArt.Metadata.Detail</p>
        }
    }

    @if (CanRawDump || lastGameFolder is not null)
    {
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 4px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
            <span class="bay-meta" style="margin: 0;">💾 File name:</span>
            <input class="label-input" style="flex: 1 1 200px; min-width: 160px; font-size: 13px;"
                   value="@gameNameDraft"
                   placeholder="@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(VolumeTitle) ? "Disc title" : VolumeTitle)"
                   @oninput="OnGameNameInput"
                   @onkeydown="OnGameNameKeydown" />
            @if (lastGameFolder is not null && !isRunning && !isVerifying)
            {
                <button class="bay-btn tray-btn" style="width: auto;"
                        disabled="@(!CanRenameFinished)" @onclick="RenameFinishedGame">
                    ✏️ Rename
                </button>
            }
        </div>
        <p class="bay-subtitle" style="margin: 0 0 8px;">
            @if (gameNameNote is not null)
            {
                @gameNameNote
            }
            else if (isRunning)
            {
                <text>You can change the name while it dumps. The new name is applied when the dump finishes.</text>
            }
            else if (lastGameFolder is not null)
            {
                <text>Type a new name and click Rename to rename the finished dump.</text>
            }
            else
            {
                <text>Leave blank to use the disc title.</text>
            }
        </p>
    }

    @if (isQueuedForBatch)
    {
        <p class="bay-meta" style="margin-top: -4px; margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--amber);">
            ⏳ Queued for Multi-Drive Batch Sync -- waiting for a free slot
        </p>
    }

    <div class="tray-control">
        <button class="bay-btn tray-btn" @onclick="ToggleTray" disabled="@isTrayBusy">
            @if (isTrayBusy)
            {
                <text>⏳ Working…</text>
            }
            else if (trayIsOpen)
            {
                <text>⏏ Close Tray</text>
            }
            else
            {
                <text>⏏ Eject Tray</text>
            }
        </button>
        @if (trayMessage is not null)
        {
            <span class="tray-message">@trayMessage</span>
        }
        <button class="bay-btn tray-btn" style="margin-left: auto;"
                @onclick="OpenOutputFolder"
                title="@(lastOutputFolder is not null ? "Open Last Output Folder" : "Open Output Folder")">
            📂 Output Folder
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="bay-actions">
        <button class="bay-btn bd @(selectedMode == "Blu-ray / 4K UHD" ? "selected" : "")"
                disabled="@(Category != DiscCategory.BluRay)"
                title="@(Category != DiscCategory.BluRay ? "Insert a Blu-ray/4K disc to enable this" : "")"
                @onclick='() => OpenModeDialog("bd")'>
            🎬 Blu-ray / 4K UHD (MakeMKV Backup Decrypt)
        </button>
        <button class="bay-btn dvd @(selectedMode == "DVD Movie Disc" ? "selected" : "")"
                disabled="@(Category != DiscCategory.Dvd)"
                title="@(Category != DiscCategory.Dvd ? "Insert a DVD to enable this" : "")"
                @onclick='() => OpenModeDialog("dvd")'>
            📀 DVD Movie Disc (ISO Dump / Movie-Only MKV)
        </button>
        <button class="bay-btn game @(selectedMode == "Game Disc" ? "selected" : "")"
                disabled="@(!CanRawDump)"
                title="@(!CanRawDump ? "Insert a game or data disc to enable this" : Category == DiscCategory.Unknown ? "Unrecognized disc (e.g. a PC game) -- dumps a raw image with Redumper" : "")"
                @onclick='() => StartGated(() => RunRedumperDump("Game", "Game Disc", "Games"))'>
            🎮 Game Disc / Raw ISO (Redumper)
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="bay-status">
        <span>
            <span class="standby-dot" style="background: @(MediaPresent ? "var(--success)" : "var(--text-muted))")"></span>
            @StatusText
        </span>
        <span>
            @if (isResolving)
            {
                <text>Resolving MakeMKV disc index…</text>
            }
            else if (notBuiltMessage is not null)
            {
                <span style="color: var(--amber);">@notBuiltMessage</span>
            }
            else if (redumperResult is not null)
            {
                @if (isRunning)
                {
                    <text>@runningLabel</text>
                }
                else if (wasCancelled)
                {
                    <span style="color: var(--danger);">● CANCELED &amp; CLEANED UP</span>
                }
                else if (redumperResult.Success)
                {
                    <span style="color: var(--success);">ISO dumped: @redumperResult.IsoPath</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span style="color: var(--danger);">@redumperResult.ErrorMessage</span>
                }
            }
            else if (makeMkvResult is not null)
            {
                @if (!makeMkvResult.Success)
                {
                    <span style="color: var(--danger);">@makeMkvResult.ErrorMessage</span>
                }
                else if (isRunning)
                {
                    <text>@runningLabel</text>
                }
                else if (wasCancelled)
                {
                    <span style="color: var(--danger);">● CANCELED &amp; CLEANED UP</span>
                }
                else if (backupResult is not null)
                {
                    @if (backupResult.Success)
                    {
                        <span style="color: var(--success);">Backup complete: @backupResult.OutputFolder</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <span style="color: var(--danger);">@backupResult.ErrorMessage</span>
                    }
                }
                else if (movieOnlyResult is not null)
                {
                    @if (movieOnlyResult.Success)
                    {
                        <span style="color: var(--success);">Movie extracted (@FormatDuration(selectedTitleSeconds)): @movieOnlyResult.OutputFolder</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <span style="color: var(--danger);">@movieOnlyResult.ErrorMessage</span>
                    }
                }
                else
                {
                    <text>MakeMKV disc index: @makeMkvResult.DiscIndex</text>
                }
            }
            else if (preflightBlockedReason is not null)
            {
                <span style="color: var(--danger);">Preflight: @preflightBlockedReason</span>
            }
            else if (selectedMode is not null)
            {
                <text>Selected: @selectedMode</text>
            }
            else
            {
                <text>@(MediaPresent ? "Disc detected" : "Ready for Disc Insertion")</text>
            }
        </span>
    </div>

    @if (batchQueueCount > 0 && !isRunning)
    {
        <p class="bay-meta" style="margin-top: 6px; color: var(--success);">
            ● BATCH QUEUE: @batchQueueCount DONE — WAITING FOR NEXT DISC
        </p>
    }

    @if (isVerifying)
    {
        <p class="bay-subtitle" style="margin-top: 4px;">Computing SHA1/MD5…</p>
    }
    else if (verificationMessage is not null)
    {
        <p class="bay-subtitle" style="margin-top: 4px; color: @verificationColor;">@verificationMessage</p>
    }
    else if (trimMessage is not null)
    {
        <p class="bay-subtitle" style="margin-top: 4px;">@trimMessage</p>
    }

    @if (isRunning)
    {
        <div class="progress-bar">
            <div class="progress-fill" style="width: @(progressPercent?.ToString() ?? "0")%"></div>
        </div>
        <p class="bay-subtitle" style="margin-top: 4px;">
            @if (progressPercent is null)
            {
                <text>Working… (no live progress available for this step)</text>
            }
            else if (runningKind == "redumper")
            {
                <text>@progressPercent%</text>
            }
            else if (runningKind == "makemkv")
            {
                <text>@FormatGb(writtenBytes) / @FormatGb(targetBytes) (@progressPercent%)</text>
            }
        </p>
        <button class="bay-btn cancel-btn" @onclick="CancelRun">✖ Cancel</button>
    }
    else if (lastAction is not null && !showModeDialog)
    {
        <button class="bay-btn retry-btn" @onclick="RetryLast">🔁 Retry Last Rip</button>
    }

    <button class="log-toggle-btn" @onclick="() => showLog = !showLog">
        @(showLog ? "▾" : "▸") Process Telemetry [@logLines.Count]
    </button>
    @if (showLog)
    {
        <div class="log-console">
            @if (logLines.Count == 0)
            {
                <div class="log-line log-empty">No activity yet.</div>
            }
            else
            {
                @foreach (var line in logLines)
                {
                    <div class="log-line">@line</div>
                }
            }
        </div>
    }
</div>

@if (showModeDialog)
{
    <div class="modal-backdrop" @onclick="CloseModeDialog">
        <div class="modal-box" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
            <h3>@(dialogKind == "bd" ? "Blu-ray / 4K UHD" : "DVD Movie Disc") — Drive @DriveLetter:</h3>
            <div class="modal-actions">
                @if (dialogKind == "bd")
                {
                    <button class="modal-btn" @onclick="ManualFullBackup">Full Backup (decrypted, everything)</button>
                }
                else
                {
                    <button class="modal-btn" @onclick="ManualFullBackup">MakeMKV Decrypted Backup (not a raw sector ISO)</button>
                    <button class="modal-btn" @onclick='() => StartGated(() => RunRedumperDump("DVD_RawISO", "DVD Raw Sector ISO", "DVD_Movies"))'>Raw Sector ISO Dump (Redumper / ImgBurn)</button>
                }
                <button class="modal-btn" @onclick="ManualMovieOnly">Movie-Only MKV</button>
                <button class="modal-btn cancel" @onclick="CloseModeDialog">Cancel</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string DriveLetter { get; set; } = "?";

    [Parameter]
    public bool MediaPresent { get; set; } = false;

    [Parameter]
    public string StatusText { get; set; } = "STANDBY // MEDIA ABSENT";

    [Parameter]
    public DiscCategory Category { get; set; } = DiscCategory.Unknown;

    [Parameter]
    public string VolumeTitle { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public string FormatLabel { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public string CapacityLabel { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public string DriveModel { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public string DriveFirmware { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public string AacsVersion { get; set; } = "";

    // Game discs only, from DiscMetadataService via AppShell: the
    // console (e.g. "PlayStation 2") and serial (e.g. "SLUS-20062").
    [Parameter]
    public string GameSystem { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public string Serial { get; set; } = "";

    // The 🎮 Game Disc / Raw ISO button (and its File name box) work for
    // recognized game discs, music CDs, and any disc the app couldn't
    // classify, such as PC game CDs/DVDs -- it's a plain Redumper dump.
    // Unrecognized discs are never auto-started, only dumped on a click.
    private bool CanRawDump =>
        MediaPresent && (Category == DiscCategory.Game || Category == DiscCategory.Unknown || Category == DiscCategory.Audio);

    // Music CDs go through the same Redumper dump (.bin/.cue per track),
    // but into their own top-level Music_CDs folder, not Games.
    private bool IsAudioDump => Category == DiscCategory.Audio || logAudioCd;

    // Set when Redumper's log shows a disc that wasn't recognized beforehand
    // is all audio tracks (a music CD) -- see MoveMusicCdFromLog.
    private bool logAudioCd = false;

    private bool? OmnidriveCompatible => DriveHardwareService.CheckOmniDriveCompatibility(DriveModel);
    private bool omnidriveConfirmed = false;
    private bool libreDriveSeen = false;

    private MetadataFetchService.CachedArt? cachedArt = null;
    private string? coverDataUri = null;
    private bool hasCachedCover => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(cachedArt?.CoverPath);
    private bool showMetadataDetails = false;

    private bool isQueuedForBatch => BatchSyncService.IsQueued(DriveLetter);

    private string? selectedMode = null;
    private bool previousMediaPresent = false;
    private bool isResolving = false;
    // isRunning / isVerifying also tell RipActivity, so an update never
    // closes the app in the middle of a rip or checksum.
    private bool _isRunning = false;
    private bool isRunning
    {
        get => _isRunning;
        set { _isRunning = value; RipActivity.Set(DriveLetter, "rip", value); }
    }
    private string runningLabel = "";
    private string runningKind = "makemkv";
    private bool showModeDialog = false;
    private string dialogKind = "bd";
    private bool wasCancelled = false;
    private string? notBuiltMessage = null;
    private string? preflightBlockedReason = null;
    private MakeMkvService.DiscIndexResult? makeMkvResult = null;
    private MakeMkvService.BackupResult? backupResult = null;
    private MakeMkvService.ExtractResult? movieOnlyResult = null;
    private RedumperService.DumpResult? redumperResult = null;
    private int selectedTitleSeconds = 0;
    private Func<Task>? lastAction = null;
    private string? lastOutputFolder = null;
    private string? trimMessage = null;

    private bool _isVerifying = false;
    private bool isVerifying
    {
        get => _isVerifying;
        set { _isVerifying = value; RipActivity.Set(DriveLetter, "verify", value); }
    }
    private string? verificationMessage = null;
    private string verificationColor = "var(--text-muted)";
    private string lastSha1 = "";
    private string lastMd5 = "";
    private string lastRedumpMatch = "";

    private long targetBytes = 0;
    private long writtenBytes = 0;
    private int? progressPercent = null;
    private string? progressFolder = null;
    private Timer? progressTimer;
    private Process? currentProcess = null;

    private bool isTrayBusy = false;
    private string? trayMessage = null;
    private bool trayIsOpen = false;

    private string? customLabel = null;
    private bool isEditingLabel = false;
    private string labelDraft = "";

    private int batchQueueCount = 0;

    // Game disc naming: the name box on the bay. Before a dump it sets
    // the name; during a dump, an edit is applied when it finishes;
    // after, the Rename button renames the finished folder and files.
    private string gameNameDraft = "";
    private string? gameNameNote = null;
    private string? lastGameFolder = null; // folder of the last finished game dump
    private string? lastGameName = null;   // name its files currently use
    private string? lastGameIso = null;    // its .iso path

    // Console found in Redumper's log after a dump (Xbox discs, which
    // Windows can't identify beforehand). GameSystem from the disc's
    // own files wins when there is one.
    private string? logGameSystem = null;

    // Disc labels that many different discs share. Saved artwork isn't
    // looked up by these, or the last game saved under "DVD_ROM" would
    // show for every disc with that label.
    private static readonly HashSet<string> GenericLabels = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
    {
        "DVD_ROM", "DVDROM", "DVD-ROM", "DVD_VIDEO", "DVDVIDEO", "DVDVOLUME", "DVD",
        "BD_ROM", "BDROM", "BD-ROM", "BDVIDEO", "BD_VIDEO", "BLURAY", "BLU-RAY",
        "CD_ROM", "CDROM", "CD-ROM", "VIDEO_TS", "PS4VOLUME", "PS5VOLUME",
        "XBOX360", "XBOX 360", "XBOX", "XBOXONE", "AUDIO CD", "AUDIO_CD", "NO NAME", "NONAME", "UNTITLED", "UNKNOWN",
    };

    private static bool IsGenericLabel(string? label) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(label) || GenericLabels.Contains(label.Trim());

    // Key for looking saved art up: the disc's name, or its serial when
    // the name is generic, or nothing (no lookup) when neither is usable.
    private string? ArtCacheKey =>
        !IsGenericLabel(VolumeTitle) ? VolumeTitle
        : !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Serial) ? Serial
        : null;

    // Where to save art: the lookup key, or the label as a last resort
    // (saved, but never auto-loaded for another disc).
    private string ArtCacheName => ArtCacheKey ?? VolumeTitle;
    private string EffectiveGameSystem =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(GameSystem) ? GameSystem : logGameSystem ?? "";

    private List<string> logLines = new();
    private bool showLog = false;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        var config = ConfigService.Load();
        if (config.BayLabels.TryGetValue(DriveLetter, out var savedLabel))
            customLabel = savedLabel;
        omnidriveConfirmed = config.ConfirmedOmniDriveLetters.Contains(DriveLetter.ToUpperInvariant());

        BatchSyncService.StateChanged += OnBatchSyncStateChanged;
    }

    private void OnBatchSyncStateChanged() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    private async Task TryAutoStart()
    {
        if (isRunning || showModeDialog) return;
        if (Category != DiscCategory.BluRay && Category != DiscCategory.Dvd && Category != DiscCategory.Game) return;

        var config = ConfigService.Load();
        bool unattended = config.UnattendedAutoStart;
        bool batch = config.BatchQueueMode;
        if (!unattended && !batch) return;

        AddLog(unattended ? "Unattended Auto-Start triggered." : "Batch Queue: disc detected, auto-starting.");

        Func<Task> pipeline = Category switch
        {
            DiscCategory.BluRay => unattended
                ? (Func<Task>)(() => { dialogKind = "bd"; return RunFullBackup(); })
                : (Func<Task>)(() => { OpenModeDialog("bd"); return Task.CompletedTask; }),
            DiscCategory.Dvd => unattended
                ? (Func<Task>)(() => RunRedumperDump("DVD_RawISO", "DVD Raw Sector ISO", "DVD_Movies"))
                : (Func<Task>)(() => { OpenModeDialog("dvd"); return Task.CompletedTask; }),
            DiscCategory.Game => () => RunRedumperDump("Game", "Game Disc", "Games"),
            _ => () => Task.CompletedTask,
        };

        if (config.MultiDriveBatchSync)
        {
            bool claimed = BatchSyncService.ClaimOrQueue(DriveLetter, config.MaxConcurrentRips, async () =>
            {
                await InvokeAsync(pipeline);
                BatchSyncService.ReleaseSlot();
            });
            if (!claimed)
            {
                AddLog($"Multi-Drive Batch Sync: queued (all {Math.Max(1, config.MaxConcurrentRips)} slot(s) busy) -- will auto-start once a slot frees up.");
                StateHasChanged();
                return;
            }
            await pipeline();
            BatchSyncService.ReleaseSlot();
        }
        else
        {
            await pipeline();
        }
    }

